<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc Rorer to mull buyout bid.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer to mull buyout bid.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Pa. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc said Thursday it intends to review the buyout offer from its majority parent Rhone-Poulenc SA at the company's regularly scheduled directors meeting on July 2.</p>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc SA said Thursday it had offered $4.3 billion for the 32.7 percent of Rhone-Poulenc Rorer it does not already own. Shares of Rhone-Poulenc Rorer rose sharply after the announcement, trading at 91-1/8 Thursday afternoon, up 11-11/16 from Wednesday's close.</p>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer had sales of $5.42 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
